  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nConsider the [PoC](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/attachment.cgi?id=9585316) from [Bug 2038800 - Content-process stack overflow: parser-built DOM cycle from `nsHtml5TreeOperation::Append` not re-validating `aParent`](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2038800):\n\nThis crashes the content process in Firefox (before my upcoming fix) and Chrome. In Safari, the `div` becomes a child of `body`, and `body` remains in its usual place in the document, but I don't find spec justification for this.\n\nPlease discuss this scenario explicitly in the spec.\n\nRight now, it's not clear to me what \"If it is not possible to insert element at the adjusted insertion location, abort these steps.\" means. What counts as \"not possible\"?\n\nI suggest explicitly saying that if _the adjusted insertion location_ is in the subtree rooted at _node_ itself, the insertion is \"not possible\". (I'm going to implement this in Firefox as the preliminary fix.)",
